---
/**
 * Three models, six matches, and a triangle that does not close.
 *
 * Every edge pools both directions: four hundred games with one model passed as A and four
 * hundred with the sides swapped. The off-policy edge carries 1 600 games because it was played
 * twice over (a second opening-book seed, both directions again) in the attempt to cross the
 * milestone's criterion; that is the published figure and the one every number here uses. Both
 * directions were run for all three pairs because the first three matches all went to whoever was
 * passed as A, and that had to be ruled out before anything could be believed. It was: swapping
 * the sides keeps the sign every time.
 *
 * Read the two top edges and the bottom one contradicts them. If the off-policy model is 65 Elo
 * above the base and the on-policy model is 57 above it, the on-policy model should be about eight
 * *below* the off-policy one. Measured head to head over 800 games, it is 37 above. The residual --
 * what the three edges fail to add up to -- is 45 Elo with a standard error of 18, at 2.6 sigma.
 *
 * That is not the intervals being generous; it is Elo doing what Elo does when the players
 * interact. A single number per model assumes strength is a total order, and a matchup is not
 * obliged to respect one.
 *
 * `labs/m5/pooled_match.py` prints these numbers and the residual from the match reports.
 */
const nodes = {
  base: { x: 320, y: 44, label: 'base', sub: 'medium-v4' },
  off: { x: 120, y: 190, label: 'DPO off-policy', sub: '6 386 pares de Lichess' },
  on: { x: 520, y: 190, label: 'DPO on-policy', sub: '6 386 pares propios' },
};

const arrows = [
  {
    from: 'off',
    to: 'base',
    text: '+65',
    sub: 'IC 50 a 81 · 1 600 partidas',
    tx: 150,
    ty: 114,
    anchor: 'start',
  },
  {
    from: 'on',
    to: 'base',
    text: '+57',
    sub: 'IC 36 a 79 · 800 partidas',
    tx: 490,
    ty: 114,
    anchor: 'end',
  },
  {
    from: 'on',
    to: 'off',
    text: '+37',
    sub: 'IC 15 a 59 · 800 partidas',
    tx: 320,
    ty: 214,
    anchor: 'middle',
  },
] as const;
---

<figure class="fig fig--intransitive" tabindex="0">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 640 268"
    role="img"
    aria-label="Tres modelos y tres enfrentamientos con las dos direcciones agrupadas. El DPO fuera de política gana al modelo base por sesenta y cinco puntos de Elo, con intervalo de cincuenta a ochenta y uno sobre mil seiscientas partidas. El DPO dentro de política gana al base por cincuenta y siete, de treinta y seis a setenta y nueve, sobre ochocientas. De esos dos se seguiría que el de dentro de política pierde con el de fuera por unos ocho puntos, y medido de frente sobre ochocientas partidas gana por treinta y siete, de quince a cincuenta y nueve. El triángulo deja un residuo de cuarenta y cinco puntos de Elo con un error típico de dieciocho, a dos coma seis sigmas."
  >
    <defs>
      <marker
        id="fig-intr-head"
        viewBox="0 0 8 8"
        refX="7"
        refY="4"
        markerWidth="7"
        markerHeight="7"
        orient="auto"
      >
        <path d="M 0 0 L 8 4 L 0 8 z" fill="var(--accent)"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>
    <g font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--muted)">
      {arrows.map((arrow) => {
        const a = nodes[arrow.from];
        const b = nodes[arrow.to];
        const dx = b.x - a.x;
        const dy = b.y - a.y;
        const length = Math.hypot(dx, dy);
        const trim = 54;
        return (
          <g>
            <line
              x1={a.x + (dx / length) * trim}
              y1={a.y + (dy / length) * trim}
              x2={b.x - (dx / length) * trim}
              y2={b.y - (dy / length) * trim}
              stroke="var(--accent)"
              stroke-width="1.3"
              marker-end="url(#fig-intr-head)"
            ></line>
            <text
              x={arrow.tx}
              y={arrow.ty}
              text-anchor={arrow.anchor}
              font-size="12"
              fill="var(--accent-text-aa)"
            >
              {arrow.text}
            </text>
            <text x={arrow.tx} y={arrow.ty + 13} text-anchor={arrow.anchor} font-size="9">
              {arrow.sub}
            </text>
          </g>
        );
      })}
      {Object.values(nodes).map((node) => (
        <g>
          <rect
            x={node.x - 80}
            y={node.y - 18}
            width="160"
            height="36"
            rx="4"
            fill="var(--diagram-stroke)"
            fill-opacity="0.14"
            stroke="var(--line)"
            stroke-width="0.9"
          />
          <text x={node.x} y={node.y - 1} text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="var(--ink)">
            {node.label}
          </text>
          <text x={node.x} y={node.y + 12} text-anchor="middle" font-size="8">
            {node.sub}
          </text>
        </g>
      ))}
      <text x="320" y="254" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9">
        la flecha de abajo debería valer −8 y vale +37: el triángulo no cierra por 45 Elo (error
        típico 18), a 2,6 σ
      </text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="caption">
    Tres aristas con las dos direcciones agrupadas: 1 600 partidas la de la izquierda, 800 las otras
    dos. Las dos de arriba predicen que la de abajo apunte al otro lado, y apunta a este.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
